uote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1345182#post1345182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooooh, interesting. That actually explains a few things. Now I think I understand the idea behind those Avarice Chronicle adventures a bit better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also that, yes,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T15:23:10-07:00","id":1345338,"title":"","content":"Since nobody has mentioned it here yet, it was recently revealed on the Discord that Nesrem is the name of one of the decrees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T17:25:42-07:00","id":1345353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in 1e pc mummies did go to Duat but no book covered it and we possibly would have seen that material if the Westward book had been reached in stretch goals. So I don't really see what 2e is doing as being a huge departure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Yes, mummies went to Duat but they almost never had any memory of the experience in play, and thus the players never got to &quot;go&quot; there either, which is more how I meant. Still, you're right in that it's possible, or probably, that the intention was to always have Duat be more interactive. After all, who's to say that in the new edition mummies remember their time there either?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1344943#post1344943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also hope the world building does a better job of reflecting the fact that the Arisen are usually in Duat and the persistent societies are being run by cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of the line in the core stating that the Mummy Guilds were even more Byzantine and Machiavellian than vampire or changeling societies. I'll never get over that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T02:19:46-07:00","id":1345411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1345338#post1345338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since nobody has mentioned it here yet, it was recently revealed on the Discord that Nesrem is the name of one of the decrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>thank you! Looking through the Discord you mentioned, I see there is a chance &quot;Nesrem&quot; Means &quot;Divine Bull,&quot; so I'm gonna make an intuitive leap and say the &quot;Ox Headed&quot; Decree of the Pillar of Ka holds the name &quot;Nesrem&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder, looking up more hieroglyphs up on a number of online, if the hawk-headed decree will be call &quot;Bak&quot; which can mean hawk.<br /> I found three hieroglyphs for snake/serpent: &quot;Aart&quot; and &quot;Nemnema&quot; and &quot;Hefau&quot; one of which could maybe be the serpent-headed decree?<br /> &quot;Khept&quot;, &quot;Her&quot;, &quot;Rema&quot;, &quot;Rebu&quot;, &quot;Ri&quot;, &quot;Ru&quot;, and &quot;Mau&quot; could all mean &quot;Lion,&quot; perhaps for the Lion headed Decree?<br /> &quot;Sab&quot; could mean &quot;Jackal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12074,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","user":"Robert D","date":". 11-02-2019, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T06:23:25-07:00","id":1345426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1345338#post1345338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since nobody has mentioned it here yet, it was recently revealed on the Discord that Nesrem is the name of one of the decrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am still proud of that guess of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T06:31:03-07:00","id":1345427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1345411#post1345411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you! Looking through the Discord you mentioned, I see there is a chance &amp;quot;Nesrem&amp;quot; Means &amp;quot;Divine Bull,&amp;quot; so I'm gonna make an intuitive leap and say the &amp;quot;Ox Headed&amp;quot; Decree of the Pillar of Ka holds the name &amp;quot;Nesrem&amp;quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder, looking up more hieroglyphs up on a number of online, if the hawk-headed decree will be call &amp;quot;Bak&amp;quot; which can mean hawk.<br /> I found three hieroglyphs for snake/serpent: &amp;quot;Aart&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Nemnema&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Hefau&amp;quot; one of which could maybe be the serpent-headed decree?<br /> &amp;quot;Khept&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Her&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Rema&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Rebu&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Ri&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Ru&amp;quot;, and &amp;quot;Mau&amp;quot; could all mean &amp;quot;Lion,&amp;quot; perhaps for the Lion headed Decree?<br /> &amp;quot;Sab&amp;quot; could mean &amp;quot;Jackal&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When Matthew permission to reveal one of the names, I chose the Nesrem because they would be the easiest to connect to the decrees. I won\u2019t say whether any of your guesses are correct for any of the others or not, but I hope that the hint will spur even more speculation. There\u2019s also a bit of a story behind the Nesrem name, but I think I\u2019ll hold off on telling it until the first KS preview drops to prevent any unintended spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/