_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1342349-what-we-know-so-far-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition?p=1345453#post1345453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit I'm not crazy about the &quot;insert Pillar, seed self in cultist&quot; idea, particularly since we already had &quot;Sacrifice Cultist to become New Body for the Arisen&quot;, but seeing it in execution might change my mind.<br /> <br /> Otherwise still quite excited for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was assuming it was actually a refinement of the good old sacrificial resurrection method...specifically limiting who can serve as the sacrifice. It kinda made sense to me since the Sadikh (a being specifically granted immortality through the use of a mummy's pillar) can serve as said sacrifice. Hoping it sort of bridging that aspect of the game with the sharing of pillars arisen can give to sorcerers from the Fall of Iseiron chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T20:58:03-07:00","id":1345516,"title":"","content":"Are the Shuankhsen coming back?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","co